## Session Summary

### Tasks
- Fixed GTK4 accent color not rendering on interactive widgets (buttons, sliders, checkboxes, radios, switches)
- Integrated Matugen (Material You color generator) to manage `gtk.css` alongside `colors.css`
- Prevented `colorreload-gtk-module` from corrupting custom widget CSS rules

### Decisions Made
- Created a static Matugen template (`gtk4-overrides.css`) containing explicit CSS widget selectors instead of trying to use template variables
- Configured Matugen to output `gtk.css` on every run, automatically restoring clean overrides and preventing colorreload corruption
- Used CSS named-color references (`@accent_bg_color`, `@dim_label_color`) defined in Material You colors to ensure theme consistency

### Files Modified
1. **`~/.config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css`** — Cleaned up (removed duplicate blocks, fixed transparent window background), now imports `colors.css` and contains explicit widget override rules for buttons, sliders, checkboxes, radios, and switches
2. **`~/.config/matugen/templates/gtk4-overrides.css`** — Created new static template with widget-specific CSS rules targeting Material You accent colors
3. **`~/.config/matugen/config.toml`** — Added `[templates.gtk4-overrides]` section to generate `gtk.css` on each Matugen run
4. **`~/.config/matugen/templates/colors-gtk4.css`** — Added `dim_label_color #9e9e9e` definition to prevent it from disappearing when Matugen regenerates `colors.css`

### Unresolved Issues
None — setup is complete.

### Next Session Context
- GTK4 theming is now fully integrated with Matugen; each `matugen` run regenerates both `colors.css` and `gtk.css`
- The accent color should now apply consistently to all interactive widgets
- `gtk.css` is automatically restored clean on each Matugen run, preventing colorreload corruption
- User can test by restarting `gtk4-widget-factory` to verify accent color displays on all widgets
